---
description: Critical Perforce (P4) version control safety guidelines and file management rules.
globs: Source/**/*, Content/**/*, Config/**/*
alwaysApply: true
---

- CRITICAL: NEVER suggest, generate, or execute a "submit", "commit", or "p4 submit" command. I must ALWAYS validate the Changelist (CL) in Unreal Engine before submitting.

# Start of work: numbered CL first
- When a new agent starts, or when the user describes a
  feature to build, create a numbered CL immediately.
- Write a short English description that names that
  feature. The default changelist cannot hold a
  description.
- Open and add files on that CL from the first edit
  (`p4 edit -c <CL>`, `p4 add -c <CL>`,
  `p4 move -c <CL>`). Do not leave work on default.
- If the user names a CL, use that number instead of
  creating another.

# New, moved, or renamed files
- If a new, moved, or renamed file belongs on the
  numbered CL of this work, `p4 add -c <CL>` or
  `p4 move -c <CL>` at once. Do not ask.
- Do not leave that file on default.

# One CL for files that depend on each other
- Do not put file A and file B on two CLs when a
  change in A only works with the change in B,
  or the other way around.
- Keep those files on the same numbered CL.
- If they must stay on two CLs because they
  implement different features, stop and tell
  the user: which files, why they depend, and
  why they stay split (two features). Do not
  move them without that warning.

# Description
- Keep the English description short and specific.
- Do not rewrite it after every edit.

# check CL
- When the user writes `check CL`, do not submit.
- Confirm every file changed in this work is open on
  that numbered CL (not default, not another CL).
  Open or add a missing file that belongs there.
  Do not ask.
- Read the CL description and the actual diffs. Update
  the description only if it no longer matches what
  was built (`p4 change -o <CL>`, then `p4 change -i`).
- Report the CL number, the files, and whether the
  description was left or corrected.
- Never submit.
